From 71a9ad10f351af1f77cff50e2965e38bd4369a7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davmels <davmelous@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:16:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Apertus 2 format: tool calls on the chat endpoint

The request's tools go into the system frame, and call frames come back as
tool calls with their arguments as written, so that a bad call reaches the
agent and its error goes back to the model. A result extends the exact tokens
of the last turn: OpenAI messages cannot hold claims or the model's own call
counters, and rollouts must stay contiguous.

vLLM's render no longer sees the messages, because it parses tool arguments as
JSON and the model may have written anything there.

Rollouts on Gym now count their tool calls and the ones the model got wrong.
---
